# Keeps the build context Railway uploads/copies small and free of
# machine-local artifacts. node_modules in particular must never be
# copied in — it was the direct cause of an EBUSY on
# apps/web/node_modules/.vite during a Railway build (a leftover local
# Vite dep-optimization cache getting carried into the image, which the
# scoped `npm ci` in railway.json then tried to reconcile against). The
# actual install always happens fresh inside the build, from
# package-lock.json — none of this should ever be needed, only shipped.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

dist/
**/dist/
build/
**/build/

.git/

# Local build/tooling caches
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
.vite/
**/.vite/
coverage/
**/coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Local-only data, never meant to leave this machine
apps/server/storage/
apps/server/prisma/dev.db
*.log

.env
.env.local
.vercel/
